.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files use JSON or JSONC format and are
.B merged
together (not replaced). Later sources override earlier ones for conflicting
keys; non-conflicting keys are preserved.
.SS Config Precedence (later wins)
.IP 1. 3
Remote config from
.B .well\-known/opencode
(organizational defaults)
.IP 2. 3
Global:
.IR ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json
.IP 3. 3
Custom (
.B OPENCODE_CONFIG
env var)
.IP 4. 3
Project:
.I ./opencode.json
.IP 5. 3
.B .opencode/
directories (agents, commands, plugins, skills, tools, themes)
.IP 6. 3
Inline (
.B OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT
env var)
.IP 7. 3
Managed configs (admin-enforced)
.SS Configuration Schema
.B opencode.json
supports the following top-level keys:
.TP
.B model
Default model in
.I provider/model
format.
.TP
.B small_model
Cheaper model for lightweight tasks (title, summary).
.TP
.B provider
Provider-specific options (timeout, chunkTimeout, setCacheKey, etc.).
.TP
.B server
Server settings: port, hostname, mdns, cors.
.TP
.B permission
Global permission rules (see PERMISSIONS section).
.TP
.B agent
Custom agent definitions (see AGENTS section).
.TP
.B command
Custom slash command definitions.
.TP
.B mcp
MCP server definitions (see MCP SERVERS section).
.TP
.B lsp
LSP server settings (true to enable, object for fine-grained config).
.TP
.B formatter
Formatter settings (true to enable, object for custom formatters).
.TP
.B instructions
Array of paths/glob patterns to additional rule files.
.TP
.B shell
Shell to use (e.g. bash, zsh, pwsh).
.TP
.B compaction
Context compaction settings: auto, prune, reserved.
.TP
.B share
Sharing mode: manual, auto, disabled.
.TP
.B snapshot
Enable/disable file change tracking for undo/redo.
.TP
.B autoupdate
Enable/disable automatic updates.
.TP
.B default_agent
Default primary agent (default: build).
.TP
.B enabled_providers
Allowlist of providers.
.TP
.B disabled_providers
Denylist of providers.
.TP
.B plugin
Array of plugin module names.
.TP
.B watcher
File watcher ignore patterns.
.SS Variable Substitution
.TP
.B {env:VARIABLE_NAME}
Substitute an environment variable value.
.TP
.B {file:path/to/file}
Substitute the contents of a file.
.SS TUI Configuration
TUI-specific settings go in
.B tui.json
(or
.BR tui.jsonc ):
.IP
.RS
.nf
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/tui.json",
  "theme": "opencode",
  "leader_timeout": 2000,
  "scroll_speed": 3,
  "scroll_acceleration": { "enabled": false },
  "diff_style": "auto",
  "mouse": true,
  "keybinds": { ... }
}
.fi
.RE
.SH AGENTS
Agents are specialized AI assistants with custom prompts, models, and tool
permissions. Two types exist:
.TP
.B primary
Main assistants you interact with directly. Switch via Tab.
Built-in: Build (all tools), Plan (read-only).
.TP
.B subagent
Specialized assistants invoked by primary agents or manually via
.BR @name .
Built-in: General, Explore (read-only codebase), Scout (external docs).
.SS Defining Agents
Agents can be defined in
.B opencode.json
under the
.B agent
key, or as standalone Markdown files in
.IR ~/.config/opencode/agents/
or
.IR .opencode/agents/ .
.P
Example Markdown agent:
.RS
.nf
\-\-\-
description: Reviews code for quality and best practices
mode: subagent
model: anthropic/claude\-sonnet\-4\-5
temperature: 0.1
permission:
  edit: deny
  bash: deny
\-\-\-
You are a code reviewer. Focus on security, performance,
and maintainability.
.fi
.RE
.SS Agent Options
.TP
.B description
(required) Brief description of the agent's purpose.
.TP
.B mode
\fBprimary\fR, \fBsubagent\fR, or \fBall\fR.
.TP
.B model
Model override in
.I provider/model
format.
.TP
.B temperature
Response randomness (0.0\-1.0).
.TP
.B top_p
Nucleus sampling (0.0\-1.0).
.TP
.B steps
Maximum agentic iterations before forced text response.
.TP
.B prompt
System prompt string or
.B {file:./path}
reference.
.TP
.B permission
Per-agent permission overrides (see PERMISSIONS).
.TP
.B color
Hex color or theme token for UI.
.TP
.B hidden
Hide subagent from @ autocomplete.
.TP
.B disable
Disable the agent.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Permissions control which actions require approval. Each key resolves to:
.BR allow ", " ask ", or " deny .
.P
Default behavior:
.B allow
for most tools;
.B ask
for
.B doom_loop
and
.BR external_directory ;
.B deny
for .env file reads.
.SS Permission Keys
.TP
.B read
Reading files (matches file path).
.TP
.B edit
All file modifications (write, edit, patch).
.TP
.B glob
File globbing (matches glob pattern).
.TP
.B grep
Content search (matches regex pattern).
.TP
.B bash
Shell commands (matches parsed command prefixes).
.TP
.B task
Launching subagents (matches subagent name).
.TP
.B skill
Loading skills.
.TP
.B lsp
LSP queries.
.TP
.B question
Asking the user questions.
.TP
.B webfetch
Fetching URLs.
.TP
.B websearch
Web search queries.
.TP
.B external_directory
Accessing paths outside the project directory.
.TP
.B doom_loop
Repeated identical tool calls (3+ times).
.SS Granular Rules
.B bash
supports object syntax for command-level granularity:
.P
.RS
.nf
"bash": {
  "*": "ask",
  "git *": "allow",
  "npm *": "allow",
  "rm *": "deny"
}
.fi
.RE
.P
The
.B last matching rule
wins. A common pattern places the catch-all
.B *
rule first and specific rules after.
.SS External Directory Access
Allow access to paths outside the project working directory:
.P
.RS
.nf
"external_directory": {
  "~/projects/personal/**": "allow"
}
.fi
.RE
.SH MCP SERVERS
Model Context Protocol servers add external tools. OpenCode supports local
and remote MCP servers.
.SS Local MCP
.RS
.nf
"mcp": {
  "my\-tool": {
    "type": "local",
    "command": ["npx", "\-y", "my\-mcp\-command"],
    "enabled": true,
    "environment": {
      "MY_KEY": "{env:MY_KEY}"
    }
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.SS Remote MCP
.RS
.nf
"mcp": {
  "sentry": {
    "type": "remote",
    "url": "https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp",
    "oauth": {}
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.P
OAuth-enabled remote MCP servers can be authenticated via:
.IP
.B opencode mcp auth \fIserver\-name\fR
.P
OAuth tokens are stored in
.IR ~/.local/share/opencode/mcp-auth.json .
.P
MCP tools are registered with the server name as a prefix, so tools can be
enabled/disabled per-agent using glob patterns (e.g.
.BR "mymcp_*" ).
