.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the TUI in the current directory
.B opencode
.TP
Start the TUI in a specific project
.B opencode /path/to/project
.TP
Continue the last session
.B opencode -c
.TP
Non-interactive prompt
.B opencode run "How does authentication work here?"
.TP
Non-interactive with file attachment
.B opencode run -f src/auth.ts "Find and fix bugs"
.TP
Continue a specific session
.B opencode -s abc123
.TP
Fork and continue
.B opencode -c --fork
.TP
Use a specific model
.B opencode -m anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5
.TP
Use a custom agent
.B opencode --agent code-reviewer
.TP
Start a headless server
.B opencode serve --port 4096 --hostname 0.0.0.0
.TP
Attach TUI to a remote server
.B opencode attach http://10.0.0.5:4096
.TP
Run commands against a running server
.B opencode run --attach http://localhost:4096 "add tests"
.TP
Export a session
.B opencode export abc123 --sanitize
.TP
Import a session
.B opencode import https://opencode.ai/s/abc123
.TP
View token usage stats
.B opencode stats --days 30 --models
.TP
List all available models
.B opencode models --refresh
.TP
Create a custom agent interactively
.B opencode agent create
.TP
Add an MCP server
.B opencode mcp add
.TP
Install GitHub integration
.B opencode github install
.TP
Upgrade to the latest version
.B opencode upgrade
.TP
Uninstall OpenCode
.B opencode uninstall
.SH TIPS
.TP
Use
.B Tab
to switch between Plan mode (no changes) and Build mode in the TUI.
.TP
Reference files with
.B @filename
to include them in your prompt.
.TP
Start a message with
.B !
to run a shell command inline.
.TP
Use
.B /undo
to revert changes (requires Git).
.TP
Commit
.B AGENTS.md
to Git for team-wide project context.
.TP
Use
.B \-\-dangerously\-skip\-permissions
only in trusted CI environments.
.TP
MCP servers add context tokens; keep enabled servers minimal.
.TP
Use
.B opencode models \-\-refresh
to update the model list after adding a new provider.
